{{short description|1887 composition by Gabriel Fauré}}
[[File:Gabriel Fauré in 1887.jpg|thumb|upright|Fauré in 1887]]
The '''Pavane''' in F{{music|sharp}} minor, [[opus number|Op.]] 50, is a short work by the French composer [[Gabriel Fauré]] written in [[1887 in music|1887]].  It was originally a piano piece, but is better known in Fauré's version for orchestra and optional chorus. It was first performed in Paris in 1888, becoming one of the composer's most popular works.
